  "evidence": "LegalZoom sells single-account legal services to \"consumers, small businesses, entrepreneurs\" (e.g. Business Attorney Plan billed annually at $469; Forms & eSign Unlimited $99/year); its site, help centre and Okta catalogue entry (SWA only) document no SSO, SCIM or user-management API.",
  "notes": "New row. LegalZoom is a consumer/small-business legal services site: subscriptions (Business Attorney Plan $39.09/mo billed annually at $469; Forms & eSign plans $59/document, $79/yr or $99/yr) attach to one customer account, with no team seats, SAML SSO, SCIM or admin API documented. The Okta OIN app is SWA (password vaulting) only; no Microsoft Learn tutorial. The public help centre (help.legalzoom.com) covers Forms & eSign and LZ Books only. No public developer API (developer.legalzoom.com does not resolve; llms.txt lists only an MCP endpoint for AI assistants). 'None' is by absence (rule 5); arguably out of scope as a single-user product.",
